# Windows Desktop App Stealth Techniques Guide

## Overview
This document outlines techniques for creating Windows desktop applications with stealth capabilities, including hiding from screenshots, screen sharing, and the taskbar. These techniques should only be used for legitimate purposes such as system administration, monitoring your own systems, or parental controls.

## ⚠️ Important Disclaimer
Applications designed to be completely hidden from detection are often associated with malware or spyware. Use these techniques responsibly and only for legitimate purposes on systems you own or have explicit permission to monitor.

